  "prompt": "This is an in-game screenshot of a portrait mobile fantasy idle RPG. Redesign ONLY its user interface into a finished, polished, cohesive mobile game UI, and keep everything else exactly as it is.\n\nKEEP EXACTLY, pixel for pixel, same size, same position, same proportions, not redrawn, not restyled: the chapter book icon, the gold coin, green star and pink pawn icons, the quest scroll, the farm location icon, the four dungeon tab icons, the whole painted terrain map with its rivers, forests, fields and castle icon, the two henchman portraits with their padlocks and tool icons, every resource icon (turnip, carrots, worm, potatoes, pitchfork, coins), and the settings cog. Keep every text label, number and its wording exactly: \"CHAPTER\", \"1\", \"0\", \"0\", \"31\", \"0/4\", \"LOCAL FARM\", \"4\", \"Farmyard\", \"Hire 31 Farm Hand\", \"930\", \"620\", \"31\", \"6\", \"4.5M\", \"4.3M\", \"MAX HIRE\", \"x64.2K\", \"Cellar\", \"+1.86K\", \"Hire 31 Rat Catcher\", \"1.55K\", \"5\", \"103K\", \"128K\", \"x1.86K\", \"Click to explore\", \"10K Crawler Scales needed to unlock the Dire Rabbit Warren\", \"0 / 10K\". Keep the exact layout: every element stays in the same place with the same width and height, nothing moves, nothing is stretched, squashed, made taller or thinner. Same 9:20 portrait frame.\n\nCHANGE ONLY the UI chrome around those assets, in stylised hand-painted fantasy (grounded adventure fantasy, not cute): the flat grey header bar and counter boxes become carved dark wood and brass plates; the brown header strip becomes painted wood planks; the flat tan LOCAL FARM tab and the dark tab buttons become bevelled wooden tabs with a brass rim; the flat grey empty hero slot becomes an ornate dark stone-and-wood card slot with a brass plus; the flat grey Farmyard and Cellar bars become bevelled leather-and-wood name plates; the flat orange Hire buttons, the orange play buttons, the teal MAX HIRE buttons and the purple portrait frames become chunky polished bevelled buttons and frames in the same colours with a soft painted highlight and darker lip; the resource slots become small bevelled item frames; the big flat orange Click to explore bar becomes a grand bevelled amber button; the flat navy background and the empty lower area become a dark warm torch-lit dungeon stone backdrop with a heavy vignette; the progress bars become inset bars with a brass rim; the bottom bar becomes painted wood. Smooth painted gradients, soft upper-left light, no black outlines, jewel-tone UI colours, muted earth tones elsewhere.\n\nRemove the debug text \"fps: 0\" and \"username\". No new elements, no extra icons, no characters, no watermark.",
